  "id": "COMPOUND:32301 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "Dodonolide is associated with MIP through multiple pathways, all of which involve the (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol compound. This compound is identified as the target of Dodonolide and is also a target of several other entities, including NCI-H446 and Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The shared target of these entities with MIP suggests a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of a common pathway or molecular target. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Dodonolide and MIP, mediated through the compound's role as a target. The consistent association across multiple paths indicates a robust, mechanistically supported relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
